ciency of the Begley home.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2009-11-18\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Gambling On Green\",\"overview\":\"Roadtrip to Las Vegas; Ed and Rachelle renew their vows at the chapel where they originally wed.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2009-11-25\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Veto Power\",\"overview\":\"Since Rachelle won't heed his calls to conserve water, Ed decides to curb water usage at the Begley household by installing a gray water system, which filters sink and shower water for reuse in his garden.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2009-12-02\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Ed's Big Birthday Bash\",\"overview\":\"Rachelle and Hayden plan a surprise party to celebrate Ed's 60th birthday. Will it be green enough for Ed, but fun enough for the planners (and attendees)?\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2009-12-09\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Author, Author\",\"overview\":\"Now that Ed has finished his second book, he and Rachelle get set to take a bite out of \\\"the big organic apple,\\\" aka New York City, for a promotional book tour.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-06\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Manners\",\"overview\":\"Rachelle and her friend decide to teach table manners to Hayden and Ed\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-13\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Love, Peace and Perry\",\"overview\":\"Ed goes to the Water Woman Festival to give a speech and ends up communing with some hippies in the desert for a couple days.  Meanwhile, Rachelle is stuck at home with Perry, a visiting overzealous entrepreneur who is pitching a lot of green product ideas that aren’t quite catching on.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-20\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"Off the Grid, On the Hook\",\"overview\":\"Ed visits Three Rivers, an off-the-grid community in Oregon, and decided he wants to retire in that area.  But Rachael does not want to move that far away from civilization.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-01-27\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"Staycation\",\"overview\":\"Ed's stay-at-home vacation turns into an ever expanding series of public appearances to help the community, leaving Rachel with the \\\"honey do\\\" chore list that Ed was supposed to do himself during his time off.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-02-03\",\"runtime\":0}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2007-01-01\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}